# Change verification

A behavior change is finished only after the nearest check passes.

- Add or extend the `*.spec.ts` next to the changed behavior.
- Run that targeted test first. Run `npm test` or `npm run build` when the change crosses domains.
- Read diagnostics for the files you edited and fix issues you introduced.
- After a domain change, run that skill's `scripts/*.mjs --check` and update its cache. The skill-script rule owns that workflow.
- Leave failures outside the task untouched.

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — prove the edit, then confirm the skill cache
npx ng test --include src/app/core/model/shapes.spec.ts
node .cursor/skills/figure/scripts/figures.mjs --check
```
